   1:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c **** /**
   2:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   ******************************************************************************
   3:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   * @file    stm32f4xx_iwdg.c
   4:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   * @author  MCD Application Team
   5:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   * @version V1.8.0
   6:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   * @date    04-November-2016
   7:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   * @brief   This file provides firmware functions to manage the following 
   8:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   *          functionalities of the Independent watchdog (IWDG) peripheral:           
   9:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   *           + Prescaler and Counter configuration
  10:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   *           + IWDG activation
  11:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   *           + Flag management
  12:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   *
  13:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****     @verbatim    
  14:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****  ===============================================================================
  15:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****                           ##### IWDG features #####
  16:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****  ===============================================================================
  17:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****     [..]  
  18:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       The IWDG can be started by either software or hardware (configurable
  19:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       through option byte).
  20:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****               
  21:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       The IWDG is clocked by its own dedicated low-speed clock (LSI) and
  22:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       thus stays active even if the main clock fails.
  23:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       Once the IWDG is started, the LSI is forced ON and cannot be disabled
  24:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       (LSI cannot be disabled too), and the counter starts counting down from 
  25:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       the reset value of 0xFFF. When it reaches the end of count value (0x000)
  26:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       a system reset is generated.
  27:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       The IWDG counter should be reloaded at regular intervals to prevent
  28:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       an MCU reset.
  29:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****                              
ARM GAS  /tmp/ccLGfcVC.s 			page 2


  30:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       The IWDG is implemented in the VDD voltage domain that is still functional
  31:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       in STOP and STANDBY mode (IWDG reset can wake-up from STANDBY).          
  32:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****               
  33:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       IWDGRST flag in RCC_CSR register can be used to inform when a IWDG
  34:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       reset occurs.
  35:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****               
  36:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       Min-max timeout value @32KHz (LSI): ~125us / ~32.7s
  37:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       The IWDG timeout may vary due to LSI frequency dispersion. STM32F4xx
  38:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       devices provide the capability to measure the LSI frequency (LSI clock
  39:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       connected internally to TIM5 CH4 input capture). The measured value
  40:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       can be used to have an IWDG timeout with an acceptable accuracy. 
  41:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       For more information, please refer to the STM32F4xx Reference manual
  42:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****             
  43:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****                      ##### How to use this driver #####
  44:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****  ===============================================================================
  45:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****     [..]
  46:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       (#) Enable write access to IWDG_PR and IWDG_RLR registers using
  47:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           IWDG_WriteAccessCmd(IWDG_WriteAccess_Enable) function
  48:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****                  
  49:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       (#) Configure the IWDG prescaler using IWDG_SetPrescaler() function
  50:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****               
  51:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       (#) Configure the IWDG counter value using IWDG_SetReload() function.
  52:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           This value will be loaded in the IWDG counter each time the counter
  53:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           is reloaded, then the IWDG will start counting down from this value.
  54:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****               
  55:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       (#) Start the IWDG using IWDG_Enable() function, when the IWDG is used
  56:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           in software mode (no need to enable the LSI, it will be enabled
  57:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           by hardware)
  58:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****                
  59:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****       (#) Then the application program must reload the IWDG counter at regular
  60:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           intervals during normal operation to prevent an MCU reset, using
  61:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****           IWDG_ReloadCounter() function.      
  62:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****             
  63:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****     @endverbatim    
  64:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   ******************************************************************************
  65:./Libraries/src/stm32f4xx_iwdg.c ****   * @attention
